  "protocol": {
    "solo": "One standing-grid time trial per model and track; 300 game-second cap.",
    "duel": "One shared-world race per grid assignment on each track; two identical Tux karts; same cameras, controls and guidance; first finisher wins. Both choose before advancing the clock. A cap without a finisher has no winner.",
    "randomized": "Ten matched development starts and four starts on two untouched tracks. Setup uses deterministic, model-independent controls near the starting line. Reported times begin at model takeover; these are not entirely model-driven standing-grid laps.",
    "timing": "Game durations count controlled simulation ticks after the fixed countdown. API waiting time is excluded. Engine finish times break crossings in the same control interval.",
    "metrics": "Rescues count button presses. Speed durations are estimates from 0.2-second samples. Slow movement can be useful cornering and is not a penalty score."
